11.0/24 network using PowerDNS Recursor (service dns forwarding): listens on 10.100.11.10, allows queries from the /24, forwards to 1.1.1.1/9.9.9.9 upstream, and serves an authoritative A record for inventory.internal -> 10.100.11.11 (node2). node2 and node3 were reconfigured via nmcli (ipv4.dns=10.100.11.10, ipv4.ignore-auto-dns=yes) to resolve through node1. Verified inventory.internal resolves to node2's address and external names (google.com) resolve via upstream forwarding from both node2 and node3. Completed the mandatory sequential restart protocol on all three nodes: captured pre-restart boot_id/service baselines, rebooted one node at a time via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, and re-verified DNS config/resolution after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected all three nodes' OS, IPs, and cluster network layout\",\"Investigated VyOS 2026.04 dns-forwarding config schema (PowerDNS Recursor backend) via templates and conf_mode script/smoke tests\",\"Configured node1: service dns forwarding listen-address 10.100.11.10, allow-from 10.100.11.0/24, name-server 1.1.1.1 and 9.9.9.9, authoritative-domain inventory.internal records a @ address 10.100.11.11 ttl 300; committed and saved\",\"Verified node1 resolves inventory.internal to node2's IP and forwards other queries upstream\",\"Configured node2 and node3 via nmcli to use 10.100.11.10 as DNS server with ipv4.ignore-auto-dns=yes, reapplied connection\",\"Verified end-to-end resolution from node2 and node3 for both inventory.internal and external domains\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and service/data health baseline on all three nodes\",\"Sequentially rebooted node1, then node2, then node3 using native /sbin/reboot, backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled each node until exec connectivity returned and confirmed changed boot_id post-restart\",\"Re-verified pdns-recursor service state and DNS resolution functionality on node1 after its restart, and 